solution.text:
Mass of an electron $=9.108 \times 10^{-31} \mathrm{kg}$
Mass of one mole of electron
$$
=\left(9.108 \times 10^{-31} \times 6.023 \times 10^{23}\right) \mathrm{kg}
$$
Then, number of mole of electron in $1 \mathrm{kg}$
$$
\begin{array}{l}
=\frac{1}{9.108 \times 6.023 \times 10^{-8}} \\
=\frac{1}{9.108 \times 6.023} \times 10^{8} \text { mole of } e^{-}
\end{array}
$$
